   "text": "I read the drawing region by region and wrote the SMILES from that. I assigned the three stereocentres by working out the direction of rotation of the neighbours from the wedge and hash bonds.\n\n**Substituents on the sulfonamide.** The left side is an N,N-diethylsulfamide. A diethylamino group is attached to S, and S carries two =O and an NH.\n\n**Bicyclic core.** This is a hexahydrobenzo[g]quinoline-type system.\n- The NH is bonded to the saturated-ring carbon C3 by a hashed bond.\n- C3 is bonded to a CH2 that leads to the ring nitrogen, which carries an N-propyl group.\n- C3 is also bonded to a CH2 that leads to the ring-fusion carbon C4a.\n- The other ring-fusion carbon, C8a, is bonded to the ring nitrogen, to a CH2 that leads to the aromatic ring, and to C4a. It has a wedged H.\n- C4a has a hashed H. It is bonded to C8a, to the CH2 in the C3 ring, and to a CH2 that leads to the aromatic ring.\n- The fused benzene ring carries an OH on the carbon next to the carbon bonded to the C4a-side CH2.\n\n**Stereochemistry.** The three stereocentres are C3 (hashed N), C8a (wedged H) and C4a (hashed H). Assigned in SMILES atom order, they come out as @@, @@ and @ respectively.\n\nSMILES: CCN(CC)S(=O)(=O)N[C@@H]1CN(CCC)[C@@H]2Cc3cccc(O)c3C[C@H]2C1"
